  "instruction": "Using Visual Studio Code, create a Python script named `burn_variability.py` in the `/home/user/analysis_results/` directory. Connect to the SQLite database `meal.db` located in the same directory. Load the tables `meal_metadata` and `final_data`, and merge them on `Workout_Type` using an inner join. For each row, compute `burn_ratio = Calories_Burned / expected_burn`. Then, for each `Workout_Type`, calculate the standard deviation of `burn_ratio`. Identify the workout type with the highest standard deviation (most inconsistent burn performance), print the summary in descending order of variability, and save the results to a text file named `burn_variability.txt` in the same directory.",
